WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:03.320
Everyone loves the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:00:03.320 --> 00:00:05.380
Everyone loves Keanu Reeves.

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:07.300
How long before the two shall meet?

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:13.099
In a chat with ComicBook.com's Brandon Davis,
Marvel Studios head honcho Kevin Feige revealed

00:00:13.099 --> 00:00:17.150
that the studio has had Reeves in mind for
a long, long time - and that they're just

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:20.610
waiting for the right role for the beloved
actor to present itself.

00:00:20.610 --> 00:00:24.780
Feige's remarks came in response to a line
of questioning which he's got to be used to

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:29.180
by now, as Davis wanted to know which of his
favorite actors might be up for an invitation

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:30.280
to the MCU.

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:31.920
The first name on his list?

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:36.820
None other than Keanu Reeves, who at the moment
is having something of a career resurgence.

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:39.120
"No way!"

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:40.420
Yes way!

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:42.280
With a chuckle, Feige admitted:

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:57.480
Feige went on to compare the situation to
Marvel's pursuit of another high-profile actor

00:00:57.489 --> 00:01:02.210
who recently joined the party: Jake Gyllenhaal,
whom he said the studio had conversations

00:01:02.210 --> 00:01:07.750
with, quote, "multiple times" before finally
casting him as Quentin Beck - AKA Mysterio

00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:10.440
- in the upcoming Spider-Man: Far From Home.

00:01:11.110 --> 00:01:13.560
"This is Mr. Beck."

00:01:13.570 --> 00:01:15.670
"We could use someone like you on my world."

00:01:15.670 --> 00:01:16.500
"Your world?"

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:22.100
Feige expressed his hope that the same patient
approach would eventually pay off with Reeves;

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:25.980
he conspicuously did not mention the fact
that multiple outlets have reported the star

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:30.049
to be in talks for The Eternals, which is
looking to be the first major release on the

00:01:30.049 --> 00:01:32.479
"Cosmic" side of Marvel's Phase 4.

00:01:32.479 --> 00:01:37.470
Feige's remarks are lent credence by the fact
that, way back in 2014, Reeves was rumored

00:01:37.470 --> 00:01:41.930
to be up for the title role in Doctor Strange,
a role which eventually fell into the very

00:01:41.930 --> 00:01:44.940
capable hands of British actor Benedict Cumberbatch.

00:01:44.940 --> 00:01:49.660
At the time, Reeves responded to the rumors
with a mix of excitement and trepidation.

00:01:49.660 --> 00:01:54.299
While he admitted to watching and enjoying
superhero flicks, claiming that he, quote,

00:01:54.299 --> 00:01:58.840
"...grew up on them and comics and graphic
novels," he admitted to being leery of signing

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:03.509
the kind of multiple-picture deal which Marvel
famously requires of its more high-profile

00:02:03.509 --> 00:02:04.300
stars.

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:05.600
He told Collider:

00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:30.689
At this point, Reeves doesn't have to do anything
just for the sake of doing it; the star is

00:02:30.689 --> 00:02:34.519
having the kind of moment that would make
peers green with envy if he weren't such a

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:36.640
legitimately breathtaking guy.

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:38.680
"You're breathtaking!"

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:41.960
"YOU'RE breathtaking!"

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:47.340
After rocketing to the A-list thanks to his
role as Neo in the Matrix series, Reeves spent

00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:51.739
the next decade or so appearing in decidedly
smaller projects before stumbling upon his

00:02:51.740 --> 00:02:53.980
next paradigm-shifting franchise.

00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:59.740
That would be John Wick, the insanely innovative
and box office-decimating shoot 'em up series

00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:03.400
which firmly cemented his status as an action
movie legend.

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:08.460
Reeves also made a splash this year in the
rapturously received Netflix rom-com Always

00:03:08.469 --> 00:03:14.069
Be My Maybe, and as Duke Caboom in Toy Story
4, which has blown critics out of their seats.

00:03:14.069 --> 00:03:18.719
On top of all this, he'll soon be returning
to one of his most fondly-remembered roles:

00:03:18.719 --> 00:03:23.409
that of Ted "Theodore" Logan, the time-traveling
rocker with a heart of gold, in next year's

00:03:23.409 --> 00:03:26.660
long-awaited three-quel Bill &amp; Ted Face the
Music.

00:03:26.660 --> 00:03:33.659
Oh, and he's set to appear in CD Projekt Red's
2020 video game, Cyberpunk 2077, playing - wait

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:37.080
for it - a dude named Johnny Silverhand.

00:03:37.460 --> 00:03:41.360
"Wake the f--- up, samurai.

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:44.460
We have a city to burn."

00:03:46.360 --> 00:03:51.540
The guy can seemingly do it all - so, with
the Marvel Cinematic Universe dominating pop

00:03:51.549 --> 00:03:56.859
culture like nothing else in recent memory,
the time seems oh-so-right for Feige and company

00:03:56.860 --> 00:04:00.280
to find that perfect role that they've long
been seeking for the star.

